"explanation": "A cardiac flatline, medically known as asystole, indicates a complete absence of electrical activity in the heart. Defibrillation is only effective for shockable rhythms such as ventricular fibrillation (VF) or pulseless ventricular tachycardia (VT), where chaotic electrical activity can be reset. In asystole, there is no electrical activity to reset, so defibrillation is not recommended. Instead, the standard of care is high-quality CPR (cardiopulmonary resuscitation) and the administration of epinephrine.",
